    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1358">

                <pb facs="1161" n="1057" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg1057"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 817.51/578.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Minister for
                        Foreign Affairs.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-10-08">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 8, 1913</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I have the honor, in behalf of the Secretary of State, who is at the moment
                    absent from Washington, to request you to assure His <pb facs="1162" n="1058"
                        xml:id="pg1058"/> Excellency the President of Nicaragua of our appreciation
                    of the sentiments conveyed in your telegram received October 7, the contents of
                    which will be brought to the knowledge of the Secretary.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">J. B. Moore</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
